{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512302-how-would-one-attain-a-spiritual-metamorphasis-exactly","id":1512302,"title":"How would one attain a Spiritual Metamorphasis exactly?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-21T14:30:58-07:00","id":1512302,"title":"How would one attain a Spiritual Metamorphasis exactly?","content":"In the &quot;DAV: Dark Ages Storytellers Companion&quot; it was shown that the Road of Metamorphasists has two minor paths: the Path of Flesh and the Path of Spirit. While it is clear how adherents of the Path of Flesh can progress on the Road of Metamorphosis, I'm more interested in what methods adherents of the Path of Spirit can use to advance within the road. I'm actually wondering why the writers would even include Path of Spirit as there are no published powers that I know of that would help an adherent alter their own soul.<br /> <br /> One could make the argument that necromancy might be useful, but from what I have seen, necromancy focuses primarily on commanding wraiths and zombies to do your bidding, not altering the practitioner's soul. Diablerie can help, but other than adding a few souls to the collection, increasing the chance of being taken over by one of your victims, developing a multi-personality disorder, and perhaps lowering your generation a bit, there doesn't seem to be much in the way of helping you attain a Spiritual Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> I actually wrote up a discipline quite recently that functions as vicissitude for spiritual entities such as souls, elemental spirits, etc. One could use this discipline to alter their own soul and merge it with other spiritual entities. I don't really know if it would make it into a game though, as it feels more similar to a Theme from VTR than an actual discipline.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts?\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T17:56:51-07:00","id":1512317,"title":"","content":"Much like the more physical aspects, there are a lot of different options for pursuing the Spiritual side of Metamorphosis, with abundant diversity of expression and exploration. There are definitely Disciplines that could be conducive to pursuing spiritual ascension; one of my favourite choices for a Tzimisce is, of course, Koldunism, especially the Way of Spirit/Genius Loci.<br /> <br /> However, the way you frame your question seems to focus on the idea of shaping the spirit/soul in a manner analogous to the way that Vicissitude can be used to shape the flesh. And that is one option, but it does not necessarily need to be only option. If you're willing to be more open-minded, less literal, and less attached to strict mechanics, then the concept of transforming one's spirit is something that can be fun to explore in a roleplay. It could involve adopting different personas to explore different aspects of one's inner self. It could involve vision-quests using potent hallucinogens consumed through a blood doll. It could involve rituals of fasting where you abstain from vitae until you are on the brink of torpor. The important thing with the Path of Metamorphosis is to have an idea of what the adherent seeks to Become; knowing that will help you figure out how the Metamorphosist needs to transform their soul in pursuit of their goal.<br /> <br /> One of the most obvious elements, in game mechanics and lore, would be progression on the Path of Metamorphosis itself. Presumably a Cainite high on the Path is one who has attained some degree of dark spiritual enlightenment, much in the way that vampires with High Humanity are seen as akin to saints and ascetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T00:22:05-07:00","id":1512333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512302-how-would-one-attain-a-spiritual-metamorphasis-exactly#post1512302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested in what methods adherents of the Path of Spirit can use to advance within the road. I'm actually wondering why the writers would even include Path of Spirit as there are no published powers that I know of that would help an adherent alter their own soul.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is complicated<br /> Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised, Chaining the Beast and Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition details the Path of Metamorphosis, the modern Road of Metamorphosis withc it is based on<br /> The followers belive they have the potential to transcend the constraints of the flesh.<br /> They believe that the next step is a state akin to apotheosis, which they call Azhi Dahaka, after the dragon of Persian mythology, and they will do anything \u2013 anything \u2013 to achieve it. It is a distant, lonely philosophy, removed from any needs other than the matter of sustenance. Followers should be heedless of others around them, existing only to satisfy their personal concerns, until they achieve Azhi Dahaka, which will completely separate them from rest of the world in a similar manner to an inverted Nirv\u0101\u1e47a. Metamorphosists often face a different problem from those who walk other Paths: Rather than struggling to uphold the tenets of their Path, Metamorphosists struggle to discover just what those tenets actually are, each for themselves. Most followers of the path keep a journal of sorts, classically called the Phrygian Codex, which details their journey to Metamorphosis. Codizes of Elder Metamorphosist are highly prized by their younger contemporaries.<br /> <br /> These are the basics.<br /> <br /> For most Metamorphosists, physical change <b><i>precedes</i></b> spiritual change.<br /> Some believe, despite the obvious evidence of their undead existence, that no creature possesses a soul and that the Curse of Caine represents flesh run rampant, flesh liberated from the obliterating cycle of life and death.<br /> Others hold that the soul is just the body summarized.<br /> As a result, most prize the use of Vicissitude and/or Protean for the shapeshifting powers these disciplines lend.<br /> <br /> The idea is, the form defines.. or not<br /> Many Metamorphosists - like the Eldest did after it became a Vampire - experiment with other forms, to see how the form effects their spirit, their soul<br /> And of course experiment on others<br /> For example, shape a dog to look like a cat, will it eventually start to behave as a cat?<br /> Or turn a vain, beautiful young girl the body of a hag, how it wil leffect the soul?<br /> With Auspex they can observe these changes and ducument them<br /> <br /> These are just crude examples of course<br /> <br /> To &quot;us&quot; humans spiritual transformation refers primarily to a fundamental change in the place of the sacred or the character of the sacred as an object of significance in life, and secondarily to a fundamental change in the pathways the individual takes to the sacred.<br /> For &quot;us&quot; the symptoms of spiritual transformation include heightened intuition, increased empathy and sensitivity, enhanced creativity, heightened dreams and visions, feeling a deep connection with the universe<br /> There are no power that can shape the soul - spirituality, meditation, experiments, faith even, lots of things do that<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised describes the following:<br /> <b>Soul Decoration</b><br /> Auspex 2, Obfuscate 2, Vicissitude 3 Combination Discipline<br /> The aura is a byproduct of the body. Change the body, change the soul. The body's experiences can be summed up in the aura, but this phenomenon is the product of physical forces. By fleshcrafting certain locations on the body \u2013 chakras, joints, erogenous zones \u2013 a Tzimisce with this power can paint whatever aura he chooses. Auras summarize the individual, revealing mood, the stain of diablerie, and the Curse of Caine. When under the gaze of perceptive eyes, sometimes it's better to conceal such things.<br /> <br /> There are other Disciplines that are &quot;messing with the soul:<br /> <br /> <b>Auspex</b> - No coment on this one, almost every power helps in form or another to understand your and the soul of the others<br /> <b>Presence </b>- Similarly to Auspex, its effect emotions and could shape the soul, change someone<br /> <br /> <b>Dementation 6: Devil in the Mind</b>: Remove all inhibitions and social morals while bringing impulses to the surface (Players Guide to Low Clans)<br /> <b>Dementation 6:</b>\u200b <b>Kindred Spirits:</b> Change the victims personality into your own (The Players Guide to the Sabbat - 19992 edition)<br /> <b>Dementation 7: Restructure: </b>Change a person's Nature (Guide to the Sabbat/ V20)<br /> <br /> <b>Daimonion 1</b>: <b>Sense the Sin</b>: This power allows the Baali to see into the soul of his or her victim in order to ferret out said victim's greatest moral weakness. (Vampire Storytellers Handbook/V20)<br /> <b>Daimonion 4: </b><b>Psychomachia: </b>The Baali summons an apparition of the victim's greatest fear or trauma (based on Sense the Sin) (Vampire Storytellers Handbook/V20)<br /> <b>Daimonion 6: Diabolic Lure:</b> Permanently lower a victim's Road rating (Dark Ages Companion)<br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Serpentis 6: Temptation:</b> Tempt someone into committing evil actions (The Players Guide 1991 edition)<br /> <b>Serpentis 7: Phobia:</b> Make someone irrationally afraid of something (The Players Guide 1991 edition)<br /> <b>Serpentis 7: Seed of Corruption: </b>Slowly erode someone's morals and raise suppressed desires to the surface (Players Guide to Low Clans/V20)<br /> <b>Serpentis 7: Set's Curse:</b> Transform someone's body and mind into a snake that acts as your servant (Dark Ages Companion)<br /> <b>Serpentis 8: Corruption: </b>Make someone addicted to sadistic acts (The Players Guide 1991 edition)<br /> <br /> <b>Obeah 3: </b><b>Peacemaker: </b>Soothe those around you and make them inclined to discuss any disputes peacefully (Clanbook: Salubri)\u200b<br /> <b>Obeah 5:</b> <b>Unburdening the Bestial Soul: </b>Draw out someone's soul and hold it in your mind while cleansing it, improving the subject's Path rating (The Players Guide 1991 edition - and many other editions)<br /> <b>Obeah 9: Spirit Marionette: </b>Take control of a target's soul and pantomime their actions (The Players Guide 1991 edition)<br /> <br /> <b>Animalism 3: Song of Serenity:</b> Soothe a creature, making them docile, and even help pull vampires from Frenzy.<br /> <b>Animalism 3: </b>\u200b<b>Quell the Beast</b>: Cow a mortal into a state of fear or apathy.<br /> <b>Animalism </b><b>\u200b5:</b> <b>Drawing Out the Beast: </b>When about to Frenzy, send your Beast into another person.<br /> <b>Animalism \u200b6:</b>\u200b<b> Deep Song: </b>Influence the emotional state of listeners with a song<br /> <b>Animalism \u200b6:</b>\u200b <b>Quell the Herd: </b>As Quell the Beast but on groups of mortals or animals<br /> <b>Animalism \u200b7: </b><b>Conquer the Beast:</b> Enter and leave your Frenzy at will","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T01:15:20-07:00","id":1512335,"title":"","content":"I don't really know, and it may be an underdeveloped side of Tzimisce lore in the manuals, but I would think that a spirit-focused Metamorphosist would focus on Auspex, Animalism and Koldunic Sorcery, plus combination disciplines with Vicissitude that allow to manipulate the soul somehow, like the already mentioned aura sculpting. A merit in Lore of Clans also allows to alter one's Nature, though that's useless in terms of Road advancement unless the ST allows for its purchase after character creation. Or one could develop advanced Vicissitude that targets the soul, if the generation is low enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T03:05:44-07:00","id":1512341,"title":"","content":"For Metamorphs that are focused on twisting their soul rather than body, their two main in clan disciplines will be Auspex and Animalism. Asupex lets the Tzimisci observe and understand their own souls and that of others. Animalism lets them control their own soul. I suspect that Soul focused Metamorphs are going to be more likely to pick up out-of-clan disciplines than those focused more on the flesh. Vicissitude largely handles any sort of alteration or twisting of the physical form. Meanwhile there are many Disciplines that can affect the soul. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> did a great job of listing those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T11:10:55-07:00","id":1512372,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy, distantly followed by protean, animalism, auspex and Diamonion/Valeren.<br /> <br /> Increasing your ability to performing miracles is an elevation of the soul. Protean and animalism elevates the Beast (arguably a spirit). Diamonion 6 is literally just giving yourself an infernal investment, and investing in yourself that was is indeed a &quot;metamorphosis' process. Valeren is soul focused and in older editions mirrored Diamonion somewhat.<br /> <br /> <br /> One could make the case for Abyss mysticism or some necromancy (some rituals are virtually permanent) but most would look at this as degeneration i would assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}